In this slide, you can find the equation of the torque.

37
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:29,900
In the right of this slide, we can see the link between the rotor speed and torque.

38
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:36,900
If the speed of the rotor is synchronous with the angular speed of the stator magnetic field,

39
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:43,900
no torque is produced by the motor because no current is induced in the rotor windings.

40
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:54,900
If the rotor rotates at a lower speed than the stator field, so the rotor speed is in the left part of the plot,

41
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,900
the motor runs in motoring mode.

42
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:07,900
Otherwise, if the rotor rotates at a higher speed than the stator field, so the rotor speed is in the right part of the plot,

43
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:14,900
the motor runs in generator mode.

44
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:25,900
In this plot, you can see the relationship between torque, speed and frequency of three-phase voltage or current.

45
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:36,900
For constant frequency, you can have a maximum torque that are almost the same for the frequencies, but different maximum speed.

46
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:43,900
Control switch between the frequencies to stay on the maximum torque possible for that speed.

47
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:56,900
In terms of high cost, need for maintenance and lack of startiness, the one rotor induction motor is less attractive than the squirrel cage counterpart,

48
00:05:56,900 --> 00:06:00,900
especially for electric propulsion in electric vehicles.

49
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:08,900
The squirrel cage induction motor is loosely named as the induction motor for electric vehicle propulsion.

50
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:20,900
In addition to the common advantages of commutator-less motor drives, the induction motor drives possess the definite advantages of low cost and ruggedness.

51
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:36,900
Disadvantages can generally upweigh their major disadvantage of control complexity and facilitate this technology being widely accepted for electric vehicles.

52
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:48,900
The permanent magnet motors are currently the most attractive motor drives for electric vehicle propulsion.

53
00:06:48,900 --> 00:07:03,900
For the use of permanent magnets, they can have high power density and high efficiency, but we can also have problems like the high cost and thermal instability of the permanent magnet material.

54
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:15,900
Divide the permanent magnet brushless machine in permanent magnet synchronous motor and permanent magnet PLDC machine.

55
